<%#
  contract-form.ejs — Screen 6, contract create (AS-127; the AS-47 §3.2 design).

  Built to docs/design/wireframes/screen-6-contract-create.html and its ledger,
  02-states-ledger.md §6 (with the §0 client sub-pattern). Every element the
  wireframe marks `data-wf-note` is annotation and is deliberately NOT built.

  PRESENTATION ONLY. Every decision was made in
  lib/screens/contract-form-view.js; this file branches on precomputed booleans
  and reads properties. Four properties hold over it, each a concept row in
  test/dependency-policy.test.js rather than a convention (README.md § The view
  layer):

    P1  no raw-output tag anywhere — this file has NO sanctioned raw line; the
        one in this app is contract-detail.ejs's, and this template adds none
    P2  no interpolation in an href/src/action/formaction/style attribute, no
        event-handler attribute, no script or style element
    P3  every attribute value carrying data is DOUBLE-quoted
    P4  within any start tag, every output tag sits inside an attribute value

  ONE FORM, NO action ATTRIBUTE. The page's own URL is the target. Every
  control that changes the page is a submit button named `intent`, dispatched
  server-side. There is no client-side script. The client sub-form is INSIDE
  the one form (nested forms are not HTML), so every round trip carries every
  contract value back by construction.

  THE FIELDS ARE THE DECLARATION'S. The loop below renders whatever
  lib/contracts/templates/ declares as form-sourced, by type; name=, id= and
  for= carry the declared name — a renderer-authored constant from code, never
  from a request. No hidden templateId input exists.

  THE TEXTAREA EMITS ONE NEWLINE AFTER ITS OPENING TAG (AS-127 decision 4):
  HTML drops exactly one leading newline inside a textarea, so a value that
  begins with a blank line would lose it on every re-render without it.

  THE CLIENT PICKER IS invoice-form.ejs's BLOCK, CARRIED A SECOND TIME with
  "Bill to" read "Client" and nothing else changed (AS-127 decision 2; the third
  consumer extracts it).

  NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS COMMENT: do not spell the raw-output tag or a
  closing EJS tag inside it — the dependency-policy scanner strips an EJS
  comment up to its FIRST closing tag. And keep the three words the
  minor-units concept row scans for out of this file, comments included.
-%>
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-state="<%= state %>">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Invoicing — <%= title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/tokens.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <%# Full chrome (01-screens.md §3): the nav is CONSTANT markup — a loop over
        data would put hrefs in data. Only the entries whose targets exist at
        this task's merge are rendered; Dashboard is AS-48's one-line addition
        (README.md § Obligations). %>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="container site-header__inner">
        <span class="app-label">Invoicing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
          <a class="site-nav__link" href="/invoices/new">New invoice</a>
          <a class="site-nav__link" href="/contracts/new">New contract</a>
          <form class="site-nav__signout" method="post" action="/signout">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-link">Sign out</button>
          </form>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title"><%= title %></h1>

      <%# The legal gate, as page chrome (AS-47 plan §3.6): constant copy in
          every rendered state, in addition to the notice inside the document. %>
      <div class="banner banner-warning">
        <p class="banner__title"><%= placeholder.title %></p>
        <p><%= placeholder.message %></p>
      </div>

      <% if (isSystem) { %>
        <%# S6-ERROR-SYSTEM's distinctive marker: the sentence is a literal of
            this branch. Nothing was created, so the form below, with every
            value preserved, IS the retry. %>
        <div class="banner banner-error">
          <p>Something went wrong generating this contract. Nothing was created — try again.</p>
        </div>
      <% } else if (banner !== null) { %>
        <div class="banner banner-error">
          <% if (banner.title !== null) { %>
            <p class="banner__title"><%= banner.title %></p>
          <% } %>
          <% if (banner.message !== null) { %>
            <p><%= banner.message %></p>
          <% } %>
        </div>
      <% } %>

      <form method="post">
        <div class="client-picker">
          <% if (showSelect) { %>
            <% if (showNewClientToggle) { %>
              <p class="client-picker__mode-toggle">Client:
                <button type="submit" name="intent" value="new-client" class="btn-link">add a new client instead</button>
              </p>
            <% } %>
            <input type="hidden" name="pickerMode" value="select" />
            <% if (clientError !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="clientId">Client</label>
                <select id="clientId" name="clientId" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="clientId-error">
                  <option value="">Select a client…</option>
                  <% for (const client of clients) { %>
                    <% if (client.selected) { %>
                      <option value="<%= client.id %>" selected><%= client.label %></option>
                    <% } else { %>
                      <option value="<%= client.id %>"><%= client.label %></option>
                    <% } %>
                  <% } %>
                </select>
                <span class="field-error" id="clientId-error"><%= clientError %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="clientId">Client</label>
                <select id="clientId" name="clientId">
                  <option value="">Select a client…</option>
                  <% for (const client of clients) { %>
                    <% if (client.selected) { %>
                      <option value="<%= client.id %>" selected><%= client.label %></option>
                    <% } else { %>
                      <option value="<%= client.id %>"><%= client.label %></option>
                    <% } %>
                  <% } %>
                </select>
              </div>
            <% } %>
          <% } else { %>
            <% if (showExistingClientToggle) { %>
              <p class="client-picker__mode-toggle">Client:
                <button type="submit" name="intent" value="existing-client" class="btn-link">choose an existing client instead</button>
              </p>
            <% } %>
            <% if (!hasClients) { %>
              <p>No clients yet — add one below.</p>
            <% } %>
            <input type="hidden" name="pickerMode" value="new" />
            <% if (clientError !== null) { %>
              <%# A generate with no client while adding one (the AS-46 review
                  cycle 1 D1 shape): the picker as a whole is the invalid field.
                  There is no select to mark, so the slot carries the message
                  alone and the banner's count still equals the page's markers. %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <span class="field-error" id="client-error"><%= clientError %></span>
              </div>
            <% } %>
            <% if (clientNameError !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="clientName">Client name</label>
                <input type="text" id="clientName" name="clientName" value="<%= clientName %>" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="clientName-error" />
                <span class="field-error" id="clientName-error"><%= clientNameError %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="clientName">Client name</label>
                <input type="text" id="clientName" name="clientName" value="<%= clientName %>" />
              </div>
            <% } %>
            <% if (clientEmailError !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="clientEmail">Client email</label>
                <input type="email" id="clientEmail" name="clientEmail" value="<%= clientEmail %>" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="clientEmail-error" />
                <span class="field-error" id="clientEmail-error"><%= clientEmailError %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="clientEmail">Client email</label>
                <input type="email" id="clientEmail" name="clientEmail" value="<%= clientEmail %>" />
              </div>
            <% } %>
            <% if (duplicate !== null) { %>
              <%# Non-blocking (ledger §0): nothing was refused, so this is a
                  warning INSIDE the form with both ways forward as submit
                  buttons. The match's id travels in a hidden input, never in
                  a URL; "create anyway" carries the confirmation with it. %>
              <div class="banner banner-warning">
                <p><%= duplicate.before %><strong><%= duplicate.label %></strong><%= duplicate.after %></p>
                <p>
                  <button type="submit" name="intent" value="existing-client" class="btn btn-secondary">Use this client instead</button>
                  <button type="submit" name="intent" value="add-client" class="btn-link">Create a new client anyway</button>
                </p>
              </div>
              <input type="hidden" name="duplicateId" value="<%= duplicateId %>" />
              <input type="hidden" name="clientConfirm" value="1" />
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="form-actions">
                <button type="submit" name="intent" value="add-client" class="btn btn-secondary">Add client</button>
              </div>
            <% } %>
          <% } %>
        </div>

        <%# The declared form fields, in declaration order, one branch pair per
            type. Each pair is written out (field--invalid / plain) rather than
            composing a class attribute from data. %>
        <% for (const field of fields) { %>
          <% if (field.type === 'multiline') { %>
            <% if (field.error !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <textarea id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" rows="3" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="<%= field.name %>-error">
<%= field.value %></textarea>
                <span class="field-error" id="<%= field.name %>-error"><%= field.error %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <textarea id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" rows="3">
<%= field.value %></textarea>
              </div>
            <% } %>
          <% } else if (field.type === 'date') { %>
            <% if (field.error !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <input type="date" id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" value="<%= field.value %>" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="<%= field.name %>-error" />
                <span class="field-error" id="<%= field.name %>-error"><%= field.error %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <input type="date" id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" value="<%= field.value %>" />
              </div>
            <% } %>
          <% } else { %>
            <% if (field.error !== null) { %>
              <div class="field field--invalid">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <input type="text" id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" value="<%= field.value %>" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="<%= field.name %>-error" />
                <span class="field-error" id="<%= field.name %>-error"><%= field.error %></span>
              </div>
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="<%= field.name %>"><%= field.label %></label>
                <input type="text" id="<%= field.name %>" name="<%= field.name %>" value="<%= field.value %>" />
              </div>
            <% } %>
          <% } %>
        <% } %>

        <div class="form-actions">
          <% if (isSystem) { %>
            <button type="submit" name="intent" value="generate" class="btn btn-primary">Try again</button>
          <% } else { %>
            <button type="submit" name="intent" value="generate" class="btn btn-primary">Generate contract</button>
          <% } %>
        </div>
      </form>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
